{"ts":"2026-10-23T14:40:12Z","session":"f6e804a3-1c28-4634-abd5-b0395560dade","prompt":"\n\n<pasted_content id=\"6a05\">\nYou are an expert full-stack engineer and product designer. I am building a take-home engineering challenge for Fathom.video (the AI meeting notetaker). \n\nThe challenge judges: Speed, Product Judgement, and UX/UI. \nCrucial constraint: The prompt explicitly allows us to FAKE/STUB the recording and capture layer. We will not build a real WebRTC recorder or connect to real AI APIs. We will use rich, realistic mock data and mock AI streams to focus 100% of our time on the post-meeting UX and advanced features.\n\n### Tech Stack\n- Next.js 14+ (App Router, TypeScript)\n- Tailwind CSS\n- shadcn/ui (Use this heavily for beautiful, accessible, fast UI)\n- Vercel AI SDK (For streaming UI text)\n- Lucide React (Icons)\n- Framer Motion (For subtle, premium animations)\n\n### The Goal\nBuild a polished, production-looking frontend that seeds a dashboard with realistic meeting data, and implements 4 advanced \"Product Judgement\" features that make the app better than the baseline Fathom.\n\n### The 4 Advanced Features to Build\n1. \"Chat with the Call\" (Conversational RAG): A right-sidebar chat where users ask questions about the meeting. The AI streams an answer with clickable timestamp citations (e.g., `[04:23]`). Clicking a citation jumps the main transcript/video player to that exact moment.\n2. \"Smart Auto-Clips\": A tab that shows 3-4 AI-generated \"Smart Clips\" (e.g., \"The Budget Discussion\"). It displays a vertical (9:16) mock video player with the speaker's name and auto-scrolling transcript text acting as dynamic captions.\n3. \"Agentic Action Execution\": Next to action items, a \"Dispatch\" button. Clicking it opens a modal showing the AI drafting a perfect follow-up email or Jira ticket for that specific action item. An \"Approve\" button shows a success toast.\n4. \"The Living Deal Room\": A dashboard view that aggregates multiple mock meetings under one client (e.g., \"Acme Corp\"). It shows a synthesized \"Deal Brief\", a \"Risk Tracker\" (e.g., \"Competitor X mentioned 3 times\"), and unified action items.\n\n### Execution Plan (Do this step-by-step)\n\n**STEP 1: Foundation & Rich Mock Data**\n- Initialize the Next.js app with Tailwind and shadcn/ui.\n- Create a `lib/mock-data.ts` file. It must contain highly realistic data for:\n  - 1 \"Deal\" (Acme Corp) containing 3 different \"Meetings\".\n  - Each meeting needs: Title, Date, Duration, Speakers (with colors/avatars), a full 2-page realistic transcript with timestamps, AI Summary, 3-4 Action Items, and 3 \"Smart Clips\" with start/end times.\n- Build the core layout: A left sidebar for navigation (Dashboard, Deal Room, Settings) and a main content area.\n\n**STEP 2: The Core Meeting View**\n- Build the Meeting Detail page.\n- Left side: A mock video player (just a nice dark rectangle with a play button and a progress bar that moves).\n- Right side: The synced transcript. When the mock \"video\" plays (use a simple `setInterval` to advance a `currentTime` state), the transcript highlights the current spoken sentence.\n\n**STEP 3: Feature 1 - Chat with the Call**\n- Add a right-hand collapsible sidebar to the Meeting View.\n- Build the chat UI. When the user sends a message, use the Vercel AI SDK `useChat` (or a mocked stream) to stream a pre-written, highly realistic response.\n- Ensure the response includes markdown-formatted timestamps like `[12:45]`. Make these timestamps clickable, updating the `currentTime` state of the main video player.\n\n**STEP 4: Feature 2 - Smart Auto-Clips**\n- Add a \"Clips\" tab to the Meeting View.\n- Build a vertical (9:16 aspect ratio) video player UI. \n- When a clip is selected, simulate playback. Overlay the speaker's name at the top, and make the transcript text for that specific time range scroll up from the bottom like TikTok/Reels captions.\n\n**STEP 5: Feature 3 - Agentic Action Execution**\n- Go to the Action Items list in the Meeting View.\n- Add a \"Dispatch\" icon button next to each item.\n- Build a Dialog/Modal. When opened, show a mock \"AI Drafting...\" skeleton loader, then reveal a perfectly formatted email draft or Jira ticket based on the action item. Add an \"Approve & Send\" button that triggers a shadcn Toast notification.\n\n**STEP 6: Feature 4 - The Living Deal Room**\n- Build the `/deal/[id]` route.\n- Aggregate the data from the 3 mock meetings for \"Acme Corp\".\n- Display a clean, executive-level UI showing the \"Deal Brief\" (mocked AI synthesis), a \"Risk Tracker\" (badges showing mentioned competitors or risks), and a unified list of all action items across all 3 meetings.\n\n### Rules for you (the AI Agent):\n1. Do not try to build everything at once. Execute STEP 1 and STEP 2 first. Stop and wait for my approval before moving to Step 3.\n2. Focus heavily on UX/UI. Use shadcn/ui components (Cards, Buttons, Dialogs, Avatars, Tabs). Make it look like a premium, $100M SaaS product. Use subtle animations.\n3. Do not build real backend databases or real AI API calls. Mock everything on the frontend or via simple Next.js Server Actions that return the mock data.\n4. Ensure the app is fully responsive and looks great on desktop (the primary use case for this tool).\n\nAcknowledge this prompt, and then immediately begin executing STEP 1 and STEP 2.\n</pasted_content id=\"6a05\">\n"}
